{
    "background_story": "Puppy was a playful and adorable origami dog created by a skilled artist. Made from a single sheet of paper, Puppy was brought to life through a series of intricate folds. As the artist's hands moved deftly, Puppy began to take shape, his paper ears perking up and his tail wagging. But Puppy's existence was not just a static creation - he was designed to be interactive. With a gentle fold, his legs would move, and he could be made to sit or stand. Children loved playing with Puppy, folding and unfolding him to create new poses. As the years passed, Puppy became a beloved companion, teaching kids about patience, creativity, and the magic of transformation through the simple act of folding.",
